{
 "encounter_id": "00818",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR",
  "person_3": "NURSE"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Hello, Mrs Sharma. I'm Joy, the nurse. I'll take your measurements while you wait. Sit here. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Temperature 36.8, pulse 84, blood pressure 118 over 72, weight 62 kilos.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good morning, Mrs Sharma. What brings you in? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Thrush. Again. Itching, soreness, white discharge. Fourth time this year."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "When did it start?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Five days."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any burning when you pass urine?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Yes, outside, when the urine touches."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any pelvic pain, fever, or an unusual smell?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No pain. No fever. No smell."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any change in your periods, or bleeding between?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. All normal."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What have you used so far?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Clotrimazole cream, twice a day. And a fluconazole capsule, 150 mg, once, on Sunday."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Did it help? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A little. It came back. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any allergies to medicines?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No allergies."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any health conditions?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'm diabetic, type 2. And I had an infection in my chest last month."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Did you take antibiotics for that? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Yes, a week of them. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Doctor, would you like me to set up the examination room? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Please, Joy. Mrs Sharma, I'll examine you now, with the nurse present. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "All right.",
   "pause": 25.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "The vulva is red and swollen, with white curdy discharge and a few small cracks, and there's no sign of any ulcers."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is it definitely thrush? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It looks typical, and the antibiotics last month and your diabetes both make it more likely. I'd say this is recurrent vulvovaginal thrush, but I can't rule out a different infection."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "What do we do? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to take a swab, to confirm it and check for other germs, and a blood test to see how well your diabetes is controlled."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "I'll take the swab now, doctor. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "For treatment, I'd like you to continue the clotrimazole for another week, and avoid scented soaps, tight clothing and douching."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll do that. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Keep a close eye on your blood sugars, because high sugar feeds thrush."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "They've been higher lately. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's something we'll look at. I'd like to see you in two weeks, with the swab and blood results."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Two weeks. Thank you. ~"
  }
